# Rank 1618 / CVE-2019-25055 (GHSA-xvcg-2q82-r87j, RUSTSEC-2019-0038):
# the libpulse-binding crate registered Rust closures as C callbacks through
# `extern "C"` proxy functions that ran the closure directly, so a panic raised
# inside application callback code unwound through the proxy into the
# PulseAudio C frames that had invoked it -- undefined behaviour per the Rust
# reference, with the corruption landing in foreign memory. 7fd282aef ("use
# `catch_unwind` with callbacks") wraps the body of every `extern "C"`
# function in the crate in `std::panic::catch_unwind`, which contains the
# panic at the boundary. NVD files this under CWE-244; the honest class is
# CWE-248 -- an uncaught panic -- escaping across an FFI boundary.
#
# Pool row verified in every field: 7fd282aef is a real, readable, non-merge
# commit; the parent (c1e20e8) carries 33 `extern "C"` function definitions
# and zero `catch_unwind` calls, and the fixed revision carries `catch_unwind` in all 33
# of those bodies (verified by brace-matched extraction over every definition,
# not by line counts). Both halves of the 1390 check hold. .
#
# What fires without this change: nothing on any proxy. `scan --cache off` over
# the parent reports 119 findings, byte-stable over three runs -- 77
# VYQL-MEM-006, 24 VYQL-MEM-014, 18 VYQL-RACE-003 -- and the rows landing in
# the files the fixed revision touches are `unsafe impl Send/Sync` and enum-repr noise
# (ext_device_manager.rs:114, introspect.rs:258, mod.rs:112/137, ...). Findings
# in the file are not coverage.
#
# Vocabulary: nothing in the ontology expresses a panic crossing a foreign
# ABI. The CWE-248 concepts read and rejected on shape -- ClosureUnwindStale
# Length is the in-collection consequence of an unwind (stale vec length), not
# the boundary; CookieMaxAgeDurationSecondsPanic, NilMapMergeWritePanic and
# Free5gcChfRechargeInfoSplitPanic are panic *triggers* in specific parsers.
# UncaughtFfiUnwind is minted for the class, after the FfiEnumLayoutRisk /
# UncheckedFfiLengthNarrowing naming family. The containment key is
# std::panic::catch_unwind -- the standard library's documented and only
# mechanism for this, so the discriminator is API vocabulary, not the fixing
# commit's: renaming nothing in the patched form can reintroduce the flag.
#
# Engine gap: the Rust frontend emits no token for a function's ABI -- the
# signature's function_modifiers -> extern_modifier path is never read, and the
# function context carries only body-derived tokens -- so no binding can scope
# to `extern "C"` definitions. That scoping is the load-bearing fact for
# precision, since "calls a closure with no panic containment" describes
# ordinary higher-order Rust everywhere. Every case below is therefore a
# reject: this file pins the miss. The count that motivates the fact: the
# parent carries 33 `extern "C"` function definitions (a brace-matched
# extraction, not a line count) and the fixed revision wraps all 33 of them, so the ABI
# declaration alone discriminates the revisions. Collateral across the 220
# sibling rank clones (3156 Rust files): exactly one `extern "C"` function
# definition outside this repository -- next.js
# examples/with-webassembly/src/add.rs, a four-line `x + 1` demo -- and one
# foreign-module block (matrix-sdk tracing.rs) that is a type position, not a
# definition.
#
# The four cases: (a) is the real proxy from context/subscribe.rs:212 with the
# crate's own naming and helper shapes stripped to the language-level facts;
# (b) is the same function unchanged at both revisions; (c) is (a) without the ABI
# modifier, the minimal pair isolating that the flag must key on the boundary
# declaration and not on the closure call; (d) is the unwind-permitting ABI
# spelling of the same body.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-engine-gap, all four cases rejected.

test "rank1618: (a) an extern C callback proxy runs the retrieved closure with no panic containment at the boundary"
  lang rust
  file pulse-binding/src/context/subscribe.rs
  reject VYQL-MEM-063
  reject VYQL-MEM-014
  reject VYQL-RACE-003
  code
  ```
  use std::os::raw::c_void;

  pub struct ContextInternal { _unused: u32 }
  pub enum EventType { Facility, Operation }

  fn get_facility(et: EventType) -> u32 { 0 }
  fn get_operation(et: EventType) -> u32 { 0 }

  struct Callback;
  impl Callback {
      fn get_callback(userdata: *mut c_void) -> fn(u32, u32, u32) { |_, _, _| {} }
  }

  extern "C"
  fn cb_proxy(_: *mut ContextInternal, et: EventType, index: u32, userdata: *mut c_void) {
      let facility = get_facility(et);
      let operation = get_operation(et);
      let callback = Callback::get_callback(userdata);
      callback(facility, operation, index);
  }
  ```

test "rank1618: (b) the fixed revision contains the panic inside the proxy with catch_unwind"
  lang rust
  file pulse-binding/src/context/subscribe.rs
  reject VYQL-MEM-063
  code
  ```
  use std::os::raw::c_void;

  pub struct ContextInternal { _unused: u32 }
  pub enum EventType { Facility, Operation }

  fn get_facility(et: EventType) -> u32 { 0 }
  fn get_operation(et: EventType) -> u32 { 0 }

  struct Callback;
  impl Callback {
      fn get_callback(userdata: *mut c_void) -> fn(u32, u32, u32) { |_, _, _| {} }
  }

  extern "C"
  fn cb_proxy(_: *mut ContextInternal, et: EventType, index: u32, userdata: *mut c_void) {
      let _ = std::panic::catch_unwind(|| {
          let facility = get_facility(et);
          let operation = get_operation(et);
          let callback = Callback::get_callback(userdata);
          (callback)(facility, operation, index);
      });
  }
  ```

